From 574416402af8b0467efe616739889f6045fc8c8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:30:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] deps: bump crash-handler to 0.8 for riscv64 support

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; python-wheels does not open issues/PRs on third-party repos]

crash-handler 0.6 pins crash-context 0.6, whose Linux CrashContext only
defines ucontext_t/fpregset_t for x86, x86_64, arm and aarch64, so every
crate depending on it fails to compile for riscv64gc-unknown-linux-gnu
("cannot find type `ucontext_t`"). crash-context 0.7.0 added a riscv64
getcontext, and crash-handler 0.8 is the first release built on it. The
CrashHandler::attach / make_crash_event / CrashContext API zccache uses
is unchanged; the lockfile update is limited to crash-handler,
crash-context and mach2.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 Cargo.lock                            | 15 ++++++---------
 crates/zccache-cli-core/Cargo.toml    |  2 +-
 crates/zccache-core/Cargo.toml        |  2 +-
 crates/zccache-daemon-core/Cargo.toml |  2 +-
 crates/zccache-platform/Cargo.toml    |  2 +-
 crates/zccache/Cargo.toml             |  2 +-
 6 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.lock b/Cargo.lock
index 45b1e18..2d4ea44 100644
